**Not this wave:** full IFC, `${}` (5.8), 2.10 user `__sec_sink__`, product `print` API, wasm/vm print lattice, check-cache versioning as the 2.9 close, M1–M20.

## Constraints (hard)

1. **Path A only** — named-sink refuse, not “perfect taint.”
2. **Rank: unify call sites vs prove existing dual refuse.** One winner. No “do both architectures.”
3. **Do not greenwash 2.9 from DE2.9 comments.** The walker does **not** call `c_secret_emit_guard`. Close only on **static map + immune smoke**.
4. **LLVM has no emit_guard.** Deleting the check/llvm front-door “because emit_guard exists” is an **FN** on `emit-llvm`.
5. **Stmt `println` is not a C call.** Forcing `c_secret_emit_guard` there needs a **fake** joined `args` string (re-lexer theater) or a product rewrite of `oo_print_*`.
6. **`c_secret_emit_guard` takes C arg texts**, not toks. Check calling it is the **wrong signature** (DE2.9 literal).
7. **Keep dual-path honesty.** Token IDENT (check + stmt println + llvm front-door) ≠ C-text belt (eprintln / free-call).
8. **Reuse fixtures.** Prefer `secret_sink_*` / `secret_eprintln_*` / `secret_multi_arg_println_fail` / `secret_t1_alias_println` + TMPDIR. Few new files.
9. **Smoke CWD must be cache-clean** (or unique content + `cd` TMPDIR). Do not trust a workspace `.ooda-cache`.
10. **Line pressure** — no new monofile; do not grow sink lists “for completeness.”
11. **Fairy writes ideas only** — DE owns land + prove.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)

Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves 2.9 MED (unproved unify / unproved dual refuse) |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no “walker calls emit_guard”; llvm not a silent belt |
| **Smoke** | Cheap: println+eprintln dual refuse; string FP; alias; static map |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (DE2.9 lie, check-only eprintln smoke, cache-false-OK) |
| **Ship** | ≤ smoke + optional 1-line DRY; no new architecture |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

