| comment FP | TMPDIR `println(1); // api_key` | ALLOW |
| concat IDENT | TMPDIR `println("pre-" + api_key)` | REFUSE (token sees IDENT) |
| leftover `print_err` | TMPDIR | emit-c secret; check **type**; llvm **no secret** — **assert residual** (I6), not a 2.9 fail |
| leftover `print` | TMPDIR | emit-c **no** secret; llvm **no** secret — **assert residual** (I7) |
| Static 2.9 | grep | check walker **has no** `c_secret_emit_guard`; `c_emit_println` **has no** emit_guard; emit_guard list **has** println/eprintln; `c_emit_lower` **has** emit_guard |

**Helper:** `expect_secret_refuse` on **each** of check / emit-c / llvm for product names.  
**Wire:** `ci_product.sh` one line.  
**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6**  
**Why must-bundle:** Without this, “2.9 FIXED” is comment-greenwash (DE2.9 already flipped from a **non-call**). Cache-false-OK is why I2 must not run `check` from a dirty workspace CWD.

### I3 — Cheap check unify: println/eprintln → `c_secret_scan_call` ⭐ (optional)
**Shape:** Replace the inline L175–193 loop with:

`c_secret_scan_call(env, toks, i + 1, n, 0, false, sid)`

Same helper as write_file/fetch/…. **Requires LPAREN** (kills accidental scan from bare `let f = println` to a later RPAREN). Alias still works: `sid = c_secret_resolve_alias(env, id)` then `f(...)` has LPAREN.

**Do not** call `c_secret_emit_guard` here. **Do not** delete stmt `c_emit_println` refuse.

**Smoke:** I2 alias case **must** still refuse after this (proves real `__alias__`, not accidental scan).  
**Darwin:** Close 6 · Honest 9 · Smoke 7 · Entropy 7 · Ship 7 → **avg 7.2**  
**Why optional same-wave:** Real DRY + LPAREN honesty. **Not** required to close 2.9 (dual refuse already holds). Land **after** I2 green so a regress is visible. Do **not** fold “scan_call swapped” into “emit_guard unified.”

### I4 — Stmt println refuse helper → `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`
**Shape:** `c_emit_println` calls the same resolved refuse as the guard (today: raw `__sec__` via `c_secret_refuse_println_ident`). Dest-taint already tags `y` after `y = api_key`. Callee alias never enters `c_emit_println`.

**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 8 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 5 · Ship 8 → **avg 6.0**  
**Why later hygiene:** Tiny; **does not** move 2.9. Keep the println-specific error string or accept `println sink refuses` via the generic helper.

### I5 — Full emit unify: stmt println → `c_secret_emit_guard`
**Shape:** Join per-arg C texts and call `c_secret_emit_guard(env, "println", a0, a1, a2, args)` from `c_emit_println` (or delete the stmt intercept so println goes through `c_emit_lower`).

**Darwin:** Close 5 · Honest 5 · Smoke 4 · Entropy 3 · Ship 2 → **avg 3.8**  
**Why later / weak now:** Stmt println is a **multi-`oo_print_*` builtin**, not `println(args)`. A fake `args` string is a **second re-lexer** of tokens already walked. Deleting the intercept changes product lowering. LLVM still needs the check walker. This is the **expensive** side of “unify call sites.”

### I6 — Add `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog` to the check walker
**Shape:** Extend `sid == "println" \|\| "eprintln"` (or I3 scan_call list) so check/llvm refuse like emit-c. Optionally `is_known_name`.

**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 8 · Smoke 6 · Entropy 5 · Ship 6 → **avg 5.8**  
**Why leftover, not 2.9:** Live emit-c already refuses (guard list). Check type-fails. llvm fail-open. Same class as T2 `ffi_call`. Same-wave **only after** I2; do **not** call this “2.9 FIXED.”

### I7 — Treat LLVM `print` as a SECRET sink
**Shape:** Check walker + `is_known_name` include `print` (llvm already lowers it as println-shape).

**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 8 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 4 · Ship 5 → **avg 5.0**  
**Why later:** `print` is **not** a typed product API. C emit does **not** `oo_print_*` it. s71 R2. Do not promote to product sink.

### I8 — Drop check / stmt token walk (“emit_guard only”)
**Shape:** Delete inline walker and/or `c_emit_println` refuse; rely on `c_secret_emit_guard`.

**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 2 · Smoke 2 · Entropy 0 · Ship 3 → **avg 2.0 — REJECT**  
**Why dies:** `emit-llvm` **FN** (no emit_guard). Stmt `println` **never reaches** emit_guard today. Opposite of dual refuse.

### I9 — Check walker calls `c_secret_emit_guard` (DE2.9 literal)
**Shape:** `c_secret_emit_guard(env, id, …)` from `check_secret_println_sinks`.

**Darwin:** Close 2 · Honest 1 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 1 → **avg 1.2 — DISQUALIFIED**  
**Why dies:** Guard wants **C arg strings**. Check has **toks**. This is the stale eighth-sprint sentence. Theater or a compile-break.

