| Host proof | Live 2026-08-12: println **and** eprintln **BLOCK** check+emit-c+llvm | No FN to fix on product names |
| Check walker | KEEP (llvm front-door) | Cheap = I3 `c_secret_scan_call`. Literal emit_guard = **I9 die** |
| Stmt println | KEEP token refuse (`c_emit_println`) | Full unify = I5 fake `args` / delete builtin |
| eprintln emit | **Already** `c_secret_emit_guard` | Already unified |
| LLVM | **Only** check walker | Drop walker → **FN** (I8) |
| Entropy \(S\) | **Down** (untested / DE2.9 lie → proved dual) | **Up** if rewrite working rails |
| Ship this turn | **Yes** | I3 optional; I5/I8/I9 **no** |

**Ship-now decision:** **prove the dual refuse.**  
Unify that is **honest** this wave is I3 (check → `c_secret_scan_call`), **not** “everything calls `c_secret_emit_guard`.”

A stub call from check into emit_guard (I9) is **neither** side of this card — prune it.

## Dual-path map (do not collapse)

| Surface | check | emit-c | emit-llvm |
|---------|-------|--------|-----------|
| stmt `println(secret)` | inline IDENT walker | `c_emit_println` token + `__sec__` | check front-door, then builtin |
| `eprintln(secret)` | same walker | `c_emit_lower` → **emit_guard** → C-text scan | check front-door, then builtin |
| `let f = println; f(s)` | resolve `f` + walker (and/or accidental no-LPAREN) | free-call emit_guard + `__alias__` | check front-door |
| `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog` | type undefined | emit_guard **SECRET** | **no secret** (I6) |
| `print(secret)` | type undefined | **no secret** (not lowered) | builtin, **no secret** (I7) |

Path-A job of 2.9 = **prove the first three rows**. Not flatten the table.

